{
  "kanji": "財",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 財\ntitle: wealth; property\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 貝\nradicalNumber: 154\nonyomi: [ザイ, サイ, ゾク]\nkunyomi: [たから]\ndistractors: [貸, 責, 貧]\n---\n\n# 財 — wealth; property\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 貝 (no. 154) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n財 refers to wealth, property, or assets. [財布](../words/財布.md) さいふ brings that idea into an everyday\nobject: a wallet. 財産 ざいさん concerns the property or assets themselves, not their container.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** put valuables in the left 貝-shaped compartment, with 才 beside it as its label.\nThis is a way to recognize the present-day shape, not a claim about its historical construction.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| サイ | on | 財布 さいふ — wallet |\n| ザイ | on | 財産 ざいさん — property; assets |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [財布](../words/財布.md) さいふ — wallet; purse\n- 財産 ざいさん — property; assets\n\n## Notes\n\nLearn サイ in 財布 and ザイ in 財産 with the whole words; the sound is not freely interchangeable.\nIn 財, 貝 sits on the left. In [貸](貸.md), [責](責.md), and [貧](貧.md), it sits underneath.\nDo not confuse owning wealth with lending it or lacking it.\n\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1296970, 1296820.\n",
